<h1>Change log</h1>
<p>Every substantive change made in response to a source goes here: what it said, what it says now, on what grounds. The log has been public from the first day, before it held a single entry — adding it after the fact would prove nothing.</p>
<h2>Version 0.9 — 14 September 2026</h2>
<p>Publication of the demonstration version. Starting point: four instruments, six open questions in the research agenda, no primary source yet examined at first hand.</p>
<h2>What will appear here</h2>
<p>Entries will accumulate as agenda items close. Each will name the agenda item, the source that settled it, and what changed on the site. The first such change matters more than the publication itself — it proves the mechanism works.</p>
